{{also|Violet}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Purple African Violet Top.JPG|thumb|an African violet (plant)]]
{{Wiktionary:Picture dictionary/en:color}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:violet<id:plant>|tree=1|id=plant}}
{{inh+|en|enm|violet}}, {{m|enm|vyolet}}, {{m|enm|vyolette}}, from {{der|en|fro|violette}}, from {{der|en|la|viola|t=violet}} + {{m|fro|-ette}}. Cognate with {{cog|lt|violetinė|t=purple, violet}} and {{cog|es|violeta|t=purple, violet}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈvaɪ.ə.lət/|/ˈvaɪ.lət/|a=RP,GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-violet.ogg|a=RP}}
* {{hyphenation|en|vi|o|let}}, {{hyphenation|en|vio|let|nocaption=1}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪlət|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q146095}}A [[plant]] or [[flower]] of the [[genus]] ''{{ll|mul|Viola}}'', [[especially]] the [[fragrant]] {{taxfmt|Viola odorata|species}}; {{lb|en|inexact}} [[similar]]-[[looking]] [[plant]]s and [[flower]]s.
#: {{syn|en|rooster|q1=historical US}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1886|translator=H.L. Brækstad|author=w:Peter Christen Asbjørnsen|title=Folk and Fairy Tales|page=160|passage=Refreshed by their cooling bath of evening dew, the '''violets''' and other nocturnal flowers emitted a pleasant fragrance over the fields, but from the bogs and the rivulets came up now and then damp, penetrating gusts, that sent an icy chill through me.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1961|author=Harry E. Wedeck|title=Dictionary of Aphrodisiacs|publisher=The Citadel Press|location=New York|page=68|passage=Albertus Magnus, the thirteenth century philosopher and occultist, states that coriander, valerian, and '''violet''' are love producing herbs.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} A [[person]] [[thought]] to [[resemble]] ''V. odorata'', [[especially]] in its [[beauty]] and [[delicacy]].
#* {{RQ:Fry Liar|page=13|passage=‘Tom,’ he said, ‘you are looking at a crushed '''violet''', a spent egg, a squeezed tube.’}}
# The color of most violets; the colour evoked by the shortest visible wavelengths between 380 and 435&nbsp;nm, an [[additive]] tertiary colour.
#: {{color panel|8200E6}}
#: {{color panel|web violet|EE82EE}}
# [[clothes|Clothes]] and {{lb|en|ecclesiastical}} [[vestment]]s of [[such]] a [[colour]].
# {{lb|en|perfumes}} The [[characteristic]] [[scent]] of ''V. odorata''.
# {{lb|en|UK|_|dialect}} {{syn of|en|onion||vegetable}}.

