===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q39297}} A three-dimensional [[measure]] of [[space]] that comprises a [[length]], a [[width]] and a [[height]]. It is measured in units of cubic [[centimeter]]s in metric, [[cubic]] inches or cubic [[feet]] in English measurement.
#: {{ux|en|The room is 9×12×8, so its '''volume''' is 864 cubic feet.}}
#: {{ux|en|The proper products can improve your hair's '''volume'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year= 1997|page=63|title= Flavour Science: Recent Developments|editors= A. J. Taylor; D. S. Mothram|publisher= w:Elsevier|url= https://books.google.co.nz/books?id=QA6kAgAAQBAJ |isbn= 9781845698232 |passage=  Volatiles of ''kecap manis'' and its raw materials were extracted using Likens-Nickerson apparatus with diethyl ether as the extraction solvent. The extracts were then dried with anhydrous sodium sulfate, concentrated using a rotary evaporator followed by flushing using nitrogen until the '''volume''' was about 0.5 ml.}}
# {{senseid|en|Q622324}} Strength of [[sound]]: how [[loud#Adjective|loud]] it is.
#: {{syn|en|loudness<id:Q622324>}}
#: {{cot|en|pitch<id:Q118819>|timbre<id:Q176501>|tone color<id:Q176501>}}
#: {{ux|en|Please turn down the '''volume''' on the [[stereo]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Volume''' can be measured in [[decibel]]s.}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|author=w:Zohran Mamdani|title=The Full Transcript of Zohran Mamdani’s Victory Speech|date=2025-11-05|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/11/05/nyregion/mamdani-speech-transcript.html|passage=This is not only how we stop Trump; it’s how we stop the next one. So, Donald Trump, since I know you’re watching, I have four words for you: Turn the '''volume''' up.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/8VqQJ|archivedate=2025-11-05}}
# The issues of a [[periodical]] over a period of one year.
#: {{ux|en|I looked at this week's copy of the magazine. It was '''volume''' 23, issue 45.}}
# A [[bind#Verb|bound]] book.
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=1|passage=However, with the dainty '''volume''' my quondam friend sprang into fame. At the same time he cast off the chrysalis of a commonplace existence.}}
# A single book of a publication issued in multi-book format, such as an [[encyclopedia]].
#: {{ux|en|The letter "G" was found in '''volume''' 4.}}
# {{lb|en|in the plural|by extension}} A great amount (of meaning) about something.
#* {{RQ:Haggard She|passage=Ayesha wheeled round, and, pointing to the girl Ustane, said one word, and one only, but it was quite enough, for the tone in which it was said meant '''volumes'''.}}
# {{lb|en|historical}} A roll or scroll, which was the form of ancient books.
#* {{quote-book|en|year= 1985 |page= 11 |title= Hebrew Manuscript Painting|author= David Goldstein |publisher= British Library |publisher2= University of Michigan |date2= 2009-06-04 |url= https://www.google.com/books/edition/Hebrew_Manuscript_Painting/QKDWAAAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=five+megillot+scrolls&dq=five+megillot+scrolls&printsec=frontcover |isbn= 9780712300544 |passage=  The Bible comprises, according to Jewish tradition, 24 books in three major sections: the Pentateuch (''[[Torah]]''); Former and Latter Prophets, and Hagiographa (or writing). The last includes five books, Songs of Songs, Ruth, Lamentations, Ecclesiastes and Esther which are called specifically [[''megillot'']] ('''scrolls''').}}
# [[quantity|Quantity]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''volume''' of ticket sales decreased this week.}}
# A [[rounded]] [[mass]] or [[convolution]].
# {{lb|en|economics}} The total supply of [[money]] in circulation or, less frequently, total amount of [[credit]] extended, within a specified national market or worldwide.
# {{lb|en|computing}} An accessible [[storage]] area with a single [[file system]], typically resident on a single [[partition]] of a [[hard disk]].
# {{lb|en|bodybuilding}} The [[total]] of [[weight]] [[work]]ed by a [[muscle]] in one [[training]] [[session]], the [[weight]] of every single [[repetition]] [[sum up|summed up]].
#: {{q|key muscle growth stimuli}} {{cot|en|mechanical tension|frequency}}
# {{lb|en|climbing|[[bouldering]]}} A [[modular]] [[foothold]] attached to a [[climbing wall]] used for [[grip]]ping, often in [[triangular]], [[pyramidal]], or [[angular]] shapes.
# {{lb|en|graph theory}} The [[sum]] of the [[degree]]s of a [[set]] of [[vertex|vertices]].
# {{lb|en|cinematography}} A {{l|en|greenscreen|green}}/{{l|en|bluescreen|blue}}-screen {{l|en|chromakey}} {{l|en|visual effects||VFX}} {{l|en|sound stage}} surrounded by a multitude of filming cameras, to allow for {{l|en|virtual camera}} changes in {{l|en|post production}}, by filming the whole 3-D volume of a chromakey {{l|en|film set}}.
# {{lb|en|cinematography}} A {{l|en|sound stage}} {{l|en|film set}} that has walls of video monitors, substituting for an actual background, set structures, providing a changeable video {{l|en|matte painting}}. A set with a form of projected background, similar to legacy traditional {{l|en|rear projection}} and {{l|en|front projection}} sets.

