|passage=Visitations are a commonly reported afterlife phenomenon. For example, a dying patient has a '''vision''' of her mother, who has been dead for twenty years.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|by extension}} Something [[unreal]] or [[imaginary]]; a [[creation]] of [[fancy]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1690|author=w:John Locke|chapter=Of our Knowledge of the Existence of other Things|title=w:An Essay Concerning Human Understanding|volume=II|section=book III|location=London|publisher=A. Bettesworth et al.|year_published=1735|page=250|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/1735essayconcern02lockuoft#page/250|passage=For having the ''Idea'' of any thing in our Mind, no more proves the Exiſtence of that Thing, than the Picture of a Man evidences his being in the World, or the '''Viſions''' of a Dream make thereby a true Hiſtory.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|by extension}} A [[perceive]]d [[potential]] [[future]] [[event]] or [[occurrence]].
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Chappell Roan;w:Dan Nigro|authorlabel=no|title=w:Pink Pony Club|date=3 April 2020|artist=Chappell Roan|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GR3Liudev18|text=I know you wanted me to stay<br>But I can't ignore the crazy '''visions''' of me in LA}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:TIME|title=When Did On-Screen Weddings Get So Bleak?|date=May 27 2026|author=Judy Berman
|text=Gilead has always been a chilling '''vision''' of what America might become if right-wing theocrats seized absolute power and stripped women of all independence.
|url=https://time.com/article/2026/05/14/testaments-finale-red-wedding-season/
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260528000830/https://time.com/article/2026/05/14/testaments-finale-red-wedding-season/}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[ideal]] or a [[goal]] toward which one [[aspire]]s.
#: {{ux|en|He worked tirelessly toward his '''vision''' of world peace.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:Architectural Digest|date=May 2026|volume=83|issue=4|title=Big Easy Does It|author=Ingrid Abramovitch|page=22
|text=To achieve their '''vision''', they enlisted the local architectural designer Marcie Banks of Clementine Construction.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} {{cap|general}} [[aspiration]]; [[forward-thinking]]ness.
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Roland Orzabal;w:Ian Stanley;w:[[Chris Hughes (musician)|Chris Hughes]]|authorlabel=no|title=w:Everybody Wants to Rule the World|album=w:Songs from the Big Chair|year=1985|artist=w:Tears for Fears|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qs-8xYwYJAQ|text=I can't stand this indecision<br>Married with a lack of '''vision'''<br>Everybody wants to rule the—}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[religious]] or [[mystical]] experience of a [[supernatural]] appearance.
#: {{ux|en|He had a '''vision''' of the Virgin Mary.}}
