# {{lb|en|transitive}}
## To [[perceive]] (something) [[visually]]; to [[see#Verb|see]].
##* {{quote-web|en|date=13 December 2023|author=Carrie Hodgin; Brian Slocum|title=When is the Best Time to View the Meteor Shower? Everything to Know about the Geminids Meteor Shower|work=w:WXII-TV|location=Winston-Salem, N.C.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231214031351/https://www.wxii12.com/article/what-time-is-the-meteor-shower/46119256|passage=Be sure to find an area far away from the city or street lights, the darker the better. Lean back or lie flat on your back with your feet facing south and '''visualize''' as much of the sky as possible. Most meteors appear as faint streaks in the sky.}}
## To [[depict#Verb|depict]] (something) in a [[way#Noun|way]] which can be seen.
##: {{ux|en|to '''visualize''' data using a chart}}
##* {{RQ:Lawrence Phoenix|title=Morality and the Novel|page=527|passage=When [[w:Vincent van Gogh|{{quote-gloss|Vincent}} van Gogh]] paints sunflowers, he reveals, or achieves, the vivid relation between himself, as man, and the sunflower, as sunflower, at that quick moment in time. His painting does not represent the sunflower itself. We shall never know what the sunflower itself is. And the camera will '''''visualize''''' the sunflower far more perfectly than van Gogh can. The vision on the canvas is a third thing, utterly intangible and inexplicable, the offspring of the sunflower itself and van Gogh himself.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=[[w:Nicole Fleetwood|Nicole R. Fleetwood]]|chapter=Hip-hop Fashion, Masculine Anxiety, and the Discourse of Americana|editors=Harry J. Elam, Jr.; [[w:Kennell Jackson Jr.|Kennell Jackson &#91;Jr.&#93;]]|title=Black Cultural Traffic: Crossroads in Global Performance and Popular Culture|location=Ann Arbor, Mich.|publisher=w:University of Michigan Press|section=part 4 (Trafficking in Black Visual Images: Television, Film, and New Media)|page=336|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/blackculturaltra0000unse/page/336/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-472-09840-8|passage=The black male model in the hoodie references the trope of the urban black menace so clearly '''visualized''' in the ghetto action films of the early 1990s as well as in contemporary music videos.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=w:Kim Hong-hee|chapter=Chan-Hyo BAE: Living on the Borderlines|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=HzkCEAAAQBAJ&pg=PA102|mainauthor=[[w:Chan-Hyo Bae|Chan[-]hyo Bae]]|title=Existing in Costume|location=Seoul, South Korea|publisher=w:Museum of Photography, Seoul|isbn=978-89-93748-77-2|passage=By becoming a male-to-female crossdresser, Chan-Hyo BAE gains insight into his identity under dual oppression. Out of the desire to know himself better, he boldly breaks into the regional differences between the East and West, the time differences between the past and present, and the gender differences between man and woman. {{...}} Bae '''visualizes''' such differences and exposes the fallacy through his deviant, transgressional work, Existing in Costume.}}
## To [[form#Verb|form]] a [[mental#Adjective|mental]] [[picture#Noun|picture]] of (something); to [[picture#Verb|picture]] (something) in the [[mind#Noun|mind]]; to [[envisage]].
##: {{coordinate terms|en|audialize|auralize|kinesthetize|olfactorize|tactilize|tactualize}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1899|author=F. F. Leighton|chapter=‘In My Mind’s Eye, Horatio’|title=Life and Books|location=London|publisher=[[w:T. Fisher Unwin|T[homas] Fisher Unwin]]{{nb...|Paternoster Square}}|page=13|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/lifeandbooks00leiggoog/page/n25/mode/1up|oclc=561621496|passage=In our own poetry we get from [[w:Geoffrey Chaucer|{{quote-gloss|Geoffrey}} Chaucer]] the first instance of self-analysis and description, the first case of '''visualising''' self.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1921|month=October|author=w:Lynden Macassey|title=Labour and the League of Nations {{...}} [book reviews]|editor=w:Harold Cox|journal=[[w:Edinburgh Review|The Edinburgh Review, or Critical Journal]]|location=London|publisher=[[w:Longman|Longmans, Green & Co.]]; New York, N.Y.: Leonard Scott Publication Company|volume=234|issue=478|page=249|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/edinburghreviewo234londuoft/page/249/mode/1up|oclc=950902861|passage=The humanitarian, frequently ignoring hard reality, '''visualises''' one cosmopolitan community where justice and social sympathy measured in terms of some one set of units reign supreme.}}
##* {{RQ:D. Smith Castle|page=33|passage=And though I can still see the shape of her that day huddled on the steps, her back view when we were in the car, her brown tweed suit and squashy felt hat, I can't '''visualize''' her face at all. When I try to, I just see the photograph I have of her.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1950|month=September|title=Centenary of the Royal Border Bridge|journal=w:The Railway Magazine|location=London|publisher=Tothill Press|page=637|issn=0033-8923|oclc=1256058197|passage=Trains have increased in weight far beyond anything '''visualised''' when the bridge was designed, but it has never undergone any major structural alterations, and continues to carry main-line traffic without weight restriction.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1950|month=October|author=R. A. Marshall|title=Kuala Lumpur, an Important Malayan Railway Centre|journal=w:The Railway Magazine|location=London|publisher=Tothill Press|page=706|issn=0033-8923|oclc=1256058197|passage=Possible developments such as electric or diesel suburban services may be '''visualised''' when the town has grown sufficiently to justify them.}}
##* {{quote-song|en|year=1983|album=w:Powerlight|author=w:Earth, Wind & Fire|title=Miracles|text='''Visualize''' a perfect place, perfect space in your mind / '''Visualize''' rainbow's end, in golden skies / I know heaven can feel you're not far away / Let it be reality / For all not just for some}}
## {{lb|en|chiefly|medicine}} To [[make#Verb|make]] (a [[hidden#Adjective|hidden]] or [[unclear#Adjective|unclear]] [[body part]], [[process#Noun|process]], or [[object#Noun|object]]) [[visible#Adjective|visible]] by [[optical#Adjective|optical]] [[method#Noun|methods]] (such as [[endoscopy]], [[magnetic resonance imaging]], [[ultrasound#Noun|ultrasound]], or [[X-ray#Noun|X-rays]]), or other [[technique]]s.
##: {{antonyms|en|hide}}
##: {{hyponyms|en|image#Verb<pos:v>}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1949|month=June|author=Thomas W. Williams; James M. Benson|chapter=Summary|title=Preliminary Investigation of the Use of Afterglow for Visualizing Low-density Compressible Flows|series=Technical Note|seriesvolume=1900|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=w:National Advisory Committee for Aeronautics|page=1|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/NASA_NTRS_Archive_19930082570/page/n1/mode/1up|oclc=660152105|passage=An investigation is described in which the phenomena of afterglow were utilized to make visible the low-density supersonic flows of various gases. {{...}} The afterglow is shown to be effective in '''visualizing''' some of the features of the flow in this range of low densities where it is difficult or impracticable to obtain comparable results with schlieren methods.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=w:International Commission on Radiation Units and Measurements|title=Image Quality in Chest Radiography|series=ICRU Report|seriesvolume=70|location=Ashford, Kent|publisher=Nuclear Technology Publishing|page=84|isbn=978-1-870965-98-9|issn=0579-5435|passage=When small masses are to be detected, it is necessary to '''visualise''' as much of the lung as possible with as little structured noise as possible. This is accomplished with high-voltage, wide-latitude, image recording and possibly beam equalisation.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}}
